# Every text file in this repository is checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# The win-64 release leg runs .github/scripts/w2-*.sh, the shared
# release-*.sh scripts and component/nunchaku straight out of
# actions/checkout@v4 through Isabelle's bundled Cygwin bash, and reads
# component/solvers.pins, VERSION, nunchaku.opam and regress/*.nun with tools
# that do not treat CR as whitespace.  Today windows-latest leaves
# core.autocrlf off and everything arrives with LF, so the leg is green -- but
# that is a runner-image default, not a guarantee.  Measured 2026-08-25 on CRLF
# copies of the committed files:
#
#   component/nunchaku   ./nunchaku --help  ->  env: "bash\r": No such file
#   component/solvers.pins  the win-64 pins step exits 0 with CVC5_VERSION=1.3.4\r
#                        (awk's default FS is [ \t\n]+, so \r stays in the field)
#                        and the leg dies ~250 minutes later on a cvc5 URL 404
#   VERSION              release-attach.sh prints
#                        `tag 'refs/tags/v0.5.3' does not match VERSION 'v0.5.3'`
#                        -- two strings that look identical
#
# A per-extension list is what let those three through: the previous rule was
# `*.sh text eol=lf`, which pinned the files that were already safe and missed
# the wrapper the leg executes.  So pin everything instead, and let
# `text=auto` leave real binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
